# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` checks
# every file out as CRLF while Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: lf` —
# so `pnpm lint` fails on all ~135 source files locally and passes in CI, which
# is the worst possible split: the gate is red for the person who can fix it and
# green for the machine that reports it.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf, so the checkout matches what CI sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Keep it out of diffs.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
